03:07.040 --> 03:11.150
So first it is checking whether the database exists, then it drops it.

03:11.190 --> 03:16.430
I have added few comments like here we are saying creating the data warehouse, creating the schemas.

03:16.470 --> 03:18.390
And now we have a very important step.

03:18.390 --> 03:22.590
We have to go and add a header comment at the start of each script.

03:22.590 --> 03:27.870
To be honest, after three months from now, you will not be remembering all the details of these scripts

03:27.870 --> 03:29.550
and adding a comment like this.

03:29.590 --> 03:35.230
It is like a sticky note for you later once you visit this script again, and it is as well very important

03:35.230 --> 03:39.870
for the other developers in the team, because each time you open a script, the first question is going

03:39.870 --> 03:42.270
to be, what is the purpose of this script?

03:42.270 --> 03:47.750
Because if you or anyone in the team open the file, the first question is going to be, what is the

03:47.750 --> 03:50.670
purpose of this script, why we are doing this stuff?

03:50.670 --> 03:56.150
So as you can see here, we have a comment saying this script creates a new data warehouse after checking

03:56.150 --> 03:57.390
if it already exists.

03:57.390 --> 04:00.550
If the database exists, it's going to drop it and recreate it.

04:00.550 --> 04:06.430
And additionally it's going to go and create three schemas bronze, silver, gold so that it gives clarity

04:06.470 --> 04:08.150
what this script is about.

04:08.150 --> 04:10.170
And it makes everyone everyone's life easier.

04:10.210 --> 04:15.210
Now, the second reason why this is very important to add is that you can add warnings.

04:15.210 --> 04:20.290
And especially for these scripts, it is very important to add these notes, because if you run these

04:20.290 --> 04:21.370
scripts, what's going to happen?

04:21.370 --> 04:23.970
It's going to go and destroy the whole database.

04:24.010 --> 04:26.490
Imagine someone open these scripts and run it.

04:26.530 --> 04:30.490
Imagine an admin, open the script and run it in the database.

04:30.530 --> 04:34.170
Everything going to be destroyed and all the data will be lost.

04:34.170 --> 04:36.810
And this can be a disaster if you don't have any backup.

04:36.850 --> 04:41.490
